{"title":"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane. Every point in the plane is colored with one of a finite number of colors. Given a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane, the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34d0a6db39eb915264c507de9f74470a3e7c0136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(X)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> has center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bcbf1dd71b52e57e9d58e39f82ed67afbea288e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX+{\\angle AOX\\over OX}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"112\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49caec5d05517e11f8b6b07c43f0a35efcb31a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOX$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is measured in radians in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa914ed4bd30af60a82d993a58fafc8144fdf3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,2\\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that we can find a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, not on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, such that its color appears on the circumference of the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34d0a6db39eb915264c507de9f74470a3e7c0136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(X)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34883963576af2dd6cbd3db7e964529e932a11c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n},\\ n\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" /> be a sequence of positive reals such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/9/889478fb1d95d8137c6834c44ff10a3dcb331491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\sum_{n\\ge 1}a_{n}\\right)^{2}&lt;2\\pi\\ (*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"154\" height=\"57\" />. For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965ac6a39c0b4d67771c31210b98312ae2e4f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9caad91166b8e2f56fda5f30a5358c1b952165.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal C_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> be the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c2884b64760793954d73926deda4f5924367f385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"42\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Because of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d02e715e7f7195675151570530c5b62ba7b2744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, we can find points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/7/c9735b73504802ca9ae3549c52d20856c97d35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i,j}\\in\\mathcal C_{i},\\ i,j\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" /> such that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c1daa47bbfc5c38b16471e0b4a85eadb12260ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/4/f747478f4e9c3fa363888b0aa2e95deff48de4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal C(x_{i,j})=\\mathcal C_{i+j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />. We now forget about all the other points, and work only with the matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/0/510476852635ca7afe4ac38bb3dc7136a1198b89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=(x_{i,j})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose we use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> colors. There must be one, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba09e029e54f3f870b2f3256b1a02d3994fc7a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, which appears infinitely many times on the first row of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, in, say, points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c458e91e673241fa8eddb6a3e172e654d10c8f9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{1,j_{1}},x_{1,j_{2}},\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba09e029e54f3f870b2f3256b1a02d3994fc7a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> cannot appear on the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/8/3b8887b5edd7b748470f8c3cc84e1a90711658c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j_{k}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b847969e6635f23c1c7bcaf38f18cad217bf08b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Next, there is a color <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/9515528033e610b398edaaedcd0de025752fe918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> which appears infinitely often among the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c308be975d3248571d4abb5daa26e6e361f0e1a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{j_{1}+1,j_{k}-j_{1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e4194d33d81c3dd5ac49c773335504c4a7a0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. But then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/9515528033e610b398edaaedcd0de025752fe918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> cannot appear on the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/8/3b8887b5edd7b748470f8c3cc84e1a90711658c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j_{k}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> for such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Repeating this procedure, we reach a stage where we have a row of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> (infinitely many actually) on which none of our <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> colors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b3680b011be9d81a737e0878593ffc10dfe27d4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{1},\\ldots,c_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"11\" /> can appear. This is a contradiction.\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by grobber. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p610123\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO\" title=\"1984 IMO\">1984 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174701\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 168/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 895/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6785/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.680      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.680      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20539:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174701 and revision id 144017. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}